spec fp03-session-wait-bounded-by-context-lpg: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# FP03. s0 writes s and reserves its commit instant (the commit hold); s1 commits t1 through a lpg.Session
# and then waits for its own commit with a 50 ms deadline: the wait returns the context
# error instead of hanging (CLAUDE.md, context-aware blocking). After s0 publishes, the
# same wait returns at once. The control interleaving publishes s0 before s1 commits.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1b s1w s1c s1aw s0p s1aw2
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1b: lpg: Session.BeginVersionedTx
step s1w: lpg: AddNode(t1); SetNodeProperty(t1, v, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1aw: lpg: Session.Await, deadline 50ms
ERROR: deadline exceeded
step s0p: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1aw2: lpg: Session.Await, deadline 30s
final ffr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
0                |0               
(1 row)
final final: <sessionless> MATCH (n) RETURN labels(n) AS labels, n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY v, size(labels(n))
labels|name|v
------+----+-
[]    |null|1
["S"] |"s" |1
(2 rows)

starting permutation: s0w s0a s0p s1b s1w s1c s1aw s1aw2
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s0p: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1b: lpg: Session.BeginVersionedTx
step s1w: lpg: AddNode(t1); SetNodeProperty(t1, v, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1aw: lpg: Session.Await, deadline 50ms
step s1aw2: lpg: Session.Await, deadline 30s
